1
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,519
Is this the Overseas Chinese Hotel?

2
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:40,040
Yes, it is.

3
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:40,920
I have a client

4
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,959
who has been staying in room 1228 for the past few days.

5
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:44,480
No one is answering in his room.

6
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:45,560
Did he check out?

7
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:46,680
His surname is Yang.

8
00:01:47,239 --> 00:01:47,760
One moment, please.

9
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,519
Can't find it?

10
00:01:48,599 --> 00:01:49,640
May I have your name, sir?

11
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,480
Could you leave your contact information?

12
00:01:57,599 --> 00:01:58,120
Thank you.

13
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:59,079
No problem.

14
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,719
Don't tail too closely.

15
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:09,919
Stay steady.

16
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:10,840
Copy.

17
00:02:22,199 --> 00:02:23,680
Hello, buying a lottery ticket?

18
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,159
Uncle Qi.

19
00:02:29,159 --> 00:02:30,240
When did you two get together?

20
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:32,000
We've been dating for over two months.

21
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,360
I've been meaning to bring her to see you,

22
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,560
but things have just been so hectic.

23
00:02:35,439 --> 00:02:36,080
Hello, Uncle Qi.

24
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,240
Yeah, this is Uncle Qi.

25
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,159
She's lovely.

26
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,840
Her family has no genetic illnesses,

27
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,479
her parents are honest folks with no debt,

28
00:02:41,719 --> 00:02:43,599
and they can help raise your kids later.

29
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,199
That's how a good life is built.

30
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,840
I give my blessing on your parents' behalf.

31
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,439
Sit down.

32
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,199
When are you planning to get married?

33
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,439
We haven't thought that far ahead yet.

34
00:02:52,439 --> 00:02:53,639
Uncle Qi, have some water.

35
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,599
If you're going to marry, do it soon.

36
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:57,639
Otherwise, don't bother at all.

37
00:02:57,759 --> 00:02:58,639
The key I gave you—

38
00:02:58,639 --> 00:03:00,800
it's for my apartment in the Textile Mill compound.

39
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,840
A little renovating, and it's a new marital home.

40
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,680
There's a kindergarten and an elementary school nearby.

41
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,000
The location is much better than your place.

42
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,360
Thank you, Uncle Qi.

43
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,120
Quick, thank Uncle Qi.

44
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,199
Thank you, Uncle Qi.

45
00:03:10,439 --> 00:03:11,639
Don't call me Uncle Qi anymore.

46
00:03:11,919 --> 00:03:12,800
Call me Godfather.

47
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,520
Godfather.

48
00:03:15,919 --> 00:03:16,599
Go ahead, call him that.

49
00:03:17,199 --> 00:03:17,840
Godfather.

50
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,000
I'm going away on a long trip soon.

51
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,960
Like your mother, I won't be back anytime soon.

52
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,280
Whatever comes up from now on,

53
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,120
you'll have to handle it on your own.

54
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:27,639
Godfather...

55
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,199
Are my parents...

56
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:31,599
never coming back?

57
00:03:31,599 --> 00:03:33,719
Nonsense. Don't jinx them like that.

58
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:36,199
Your mother will be back in a while.

59
00:03:36,439 --> 00:03:36,919
Just wait.

60
00:03:36,919 --> 00:03:37,719
How much longer will it take?

61
00:03:37,719 --> 00:03:38,639
When exactly?

62
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,599
You'll know when the time comes.

63
00:03:41,199 --> 00:03:41,960
Save me some worry.

64
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:43,479
Live a good life.

65
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:48,919
I'm off.

66
00:03:49,919 --> 00:03:50,840
Take care, Godfather.

67
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,120
Take care, Godfather.

68
00:03:57,479 --> 00:03:58,599
Hello, buying a lottery ticket?

69
00:03:58,599 --> 00:03:58,960
Yes.

70
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,719
The same lucky numbers as last time.

71
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:01,520
Lucky numbers.

72
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:01,879
Sure.

73
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,000
I don't recognize any of these new faces.

74
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,800
I thought Wu Jiali was still driving.

75
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,040
Didn't he come?

76
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:18,680
You have to trust the newcomers.

77
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:19,720
If you say so.

78
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:21,079
By the way,

79
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:23,319
the escape route arranged by the people from Taiwan, China—

80
00:04:23,319 --> 00:04:24,399
why didn't you take it?

81
00:04:25,439 --> 00:04:26,879
Your ironclad dragnet was already set up.

82
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:28,240
I couldn't escape anyway.

83
00:04:28,519 --> 00:04:30,240
Why bother running around in circles?

84
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:32,279
Throwing my back out wouldn't be worth it.

85
00:04:34,279 --> 00:04:35,680
The hair at your temples has turned gray.

86
00:04:36,199 --> 00:04:37,079
You didn't even dye it.

87
00:04:38,959 --> 00:04:40,680
Since when does Brother Qi admit defeat?

88
00:04:41,879 --> 00:04:43,040
If you lose, you accept it.

89
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,759
I anticipated you'd make a move,

90
00:04:45,759 --> 00:04:47,360
just not that you'd strike so fast.

91
00:04:48,879 --> 00:04:49,639
Yang Shiwen must have told you

92
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:50,879
about my trip to Taiwan, China.

93
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,480
Coming to see Maozai,

94
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,879
you could've just come out in the open.

95
00:04:56,199 --> 00:04:57,040
Why did you have to hide?

96
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,959
Of course I had to hide.

97
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,879
What if Baoshan had led the team instead of you?

98
00:05:00,879 --> 00:05:01,959
He's so jealous of me,

99
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:02,680
who knows,

100
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,240
he might've arrested me right in front of Maozai.

101
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,240
Let's head out.

102
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:11,879
What are we waiting for?

103
00:05:47,839 --> 00:05:48,800
Where's Sister Xia?

104
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,399
Could you have her bring my clothes over?

105
00:05:54,639 --> 00:05:55,639
And my leather shoes, too.

106
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,160
When was the last time

107
00:06:07,439 --> 00:06:08,360
you met with Yang Shiwen?

108
00:06:08,959 --> 00:06:09,759
I don't remember.

109
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,920
You don't remember when you met?

110
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:14,360
Then what did you do when you met,

111
00:06:14,519 --> 00:06:15,639
and what did you say?

112
00:06:15,839 --> 00:06:17,000
Surely you remember that much.

113
00:06:17,519 --> 00:06:18,920
There's no such thing as "surely."

114
00:06:19,519 --> 00:06:20,680
Too much has happened,

115
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:21,800
and I'm getting old.

116
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:22,920
I'm not who I used to be.

117
00:06:23,639 --> 00:06:24,439
I really did forget.

118
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:26,839
Back when you trained your apprentice,

119
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,639
you demanded that he

120
00:06:29,759 --> 00:06:31,920
remember every single word spoken

121
00:06:32,519 --> 00:06:34,120
and every single deed done.

122
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,040
How come today, when it's your turn,

123
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,519
you can't remember a thing?

124
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,240
Only he would buy that clumsy method of mine.

125
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,600
Who else would believe it?

126
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,519
Then let's not talk about Yang Shiwen.

127
00:06:45,639 --> 00:06:47,279
Let's talk about Old Jia, Jin Chizhong,

128
00:06:47,279 --> 00:06:48,800
Xiao Lu, Cao Liaoping,

129
00:06:49,279 --> 00:06:51,040
or the people over in Taiwan, China.

130
00:06:51,319 --> 00:06:53,079
You can't avoid this by staying silent.

131
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,839
Pick whichever interests you.

132
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,639
Do you find this exhausting?

133
00:06:59,279 --> 00:07:00,959
Interrogating one of our own is the hardest.

134
00:07:01,279 --> 00:07:02,319
Know yourself and know your enemy.

135
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,560
Before you even bait the hook,

136
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,439
I already know what fish you want to catch.

137
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,000
As for you,

138
00:07:10,519 --> 00:07:11,759
I'll treat you as a new case

139
00:07:12,079 --> 00:07:13,279
to gain some experience.

140
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,680
Facing you, I still need to stay humble.

141
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:16,839
Nothing shameful about that.

142
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,600
With some people, there's no need to be humble,

143
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,480
because it's completely unnecessary.

144
00:07:20,839 --> 00:07:22,439
When are you going to drop

145
00:07:22,439 --> 00:07:24,480
that preachy, patronizing tone of yours?

146
00:07:25,439 --> 00:07:27,079
Stalling like this is pointless.

147
00:07:27,279 --> 00:07:28,639
Because the outcome will be the same.

148
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:33,759
I feel like there's something new in your eyes.

149
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,040
How should I put it?

150
00:07:37,639 --> 00:07:38,879
A hunger to destroy me.

151
00:07:39,199 --> 00:07:40,279
State security

152
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,199
is a matter of life and death.

153
00:07:42,959 --> 00:07:44,680
You think everyone is like you?

154
00:07:44,959 --> 00:07:47,040
At death's door, yet still playing it cool.

155
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,360
Ma Qi,

156
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,800
we've known each other for so many years.

157
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,120
We know everything about each other.

158
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,839
Can't we have an honest talk?

159
00:08:01,759 --> 00:08:04,120
Team Three reported back.

160
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:06,399
Ma Qi and Yang Shiwen have both gone dark.

161
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,959
They've most likely been arrested.

162
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,360
I don't want to hear "likely."

163
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,680
Confirm it before you tell me.

164
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:14,040
It's basically confirmed now.

165
00:08:14,519 --> 00:08:15,600
Right now,

166
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,720
I have to report to the top

167
00:08:18,439 --> 00:08:19,720
and analyze this.

168
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:22,120
The intel on Huanyu 10 that Ma Qi brought back...

169
00:08:22,759 --> 00:08:24,120
Such a good channel,

170
00:08:24,279 --> 00:08:26,399
and they shut it down so quickly!

171
00:08:26,519 --> 00:08:27,920
If the brass asks about it,

172
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,959
what am I supposed to say?

173
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,159
He probably won't be eliminated.

174
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,679
He was just buying and selling.

175
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,960
It won't be the death penalty.

176
00:08:35,399 --> 00:08:38,000
Once he's out, he can still be of use to me.

177
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:40,320
Have someone look into it,

178
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,080
see if we can get his sentence reduced.

179
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,000
Understood.

180
00:08:43,519 --> 00:08:45,639
Once this intelligence is put into play,

181
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:46,960
in my lifetime,

182
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,799
I'll witness another Taiwan Strait crisis.

183
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,120
And another thing, Lin Kanshan.

184
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,080
That airport or whatever over there,

185
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,320
how is that going?

186
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:57,080
It should be at the final stage.

187
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,879
Once he's done, I'll have him return to Taiwan, China.

188
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,200
But this man, Director...

189
00:09:02,639 --> 00:09:04,600
I only care about getting what I want.

190
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,519
You deal with the rest as you see fit.

191
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:07,720
Yes, sir.

192
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,360
I just got back from the hospital.

193
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,240
We've moved your father to a private room.

194
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:20,240
Section Chief Yin's brother-in-law is a director there.

195
00:09:20,399 --> 00:09:22,360
He took care of the arrangements.

196
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,440
After two surgeries,

197
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,960
it wasn't easy for him to pull through.

198
00:09:27,559 --> 00:09:29,399
But his condition hasn't stabilized yet.

199
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:31,320
Given his advanced age,

200
00:09:32,039 --> 00:09:33,639
you should prepare for the worst.

201
00:09:36,759 --> 00:09:39,240
Don't worry, I've already talked to them.

202
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:41,399
If anything happens at the hospital,

203
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:42,879
they can call directly

204
00:09:42,879 --> 00:09:43,840
to ask for your opinion.

205
00:09:47,759 --> 00:09:49,240
We've known each other for years.

206
00:09:50,039 --> 00:09:51,519
I know what kind of person you are.

207
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,240
But you should see the current situation clearly, too.

208
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:57,399
If there's anything you want to say or do,

209
00:09:57,879 --> 00:09:58,840
bring it up now.

210
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,360
This is your last chance.

211
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,240
Where's my son?

212
00:10:16,639 --> 00:10:17,879
Does my daughter know?

213
00:10:17,879 --> 00:10:19,919
You brought me here.

214
00:10:20,159 --> 00:10:21,200
When you arrest someone,

215
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,759
if you notify the family,

216
00:10:22,759 --> 00:10:24,200
will you notify her school?

217
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:26,679
Qian Wenying.

218
00:10:26,679 --> 00:10:28,840
Can you tell the nanny over there

219
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,039
to bring the formula back from my office?

220
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:33,720
It was just brought to my office.

221
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,360
They don't know yet.

222
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,039
Try it.

223
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,720
Still tastes the same, Boss Wen?

224
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,159
Aren't you going to ask about Sister Xia?

225
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,240
She can take care of herself.

226
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,279
She's fine.

227
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:33,720
She's already confessed to everything.

228
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,440
Go see my driver.

229
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,559
He has everything I've handled.

230
00:12:06,159 --> 00:12:07,399
I'd like another bowl.

231
00:12:07,879 --> 00:12:08,720
May I?

232
00:12:22,639 --> 00:12:23,960
Want some more hot water?

233
00:12:25,159 --> 00:12:26,080
What are you thinking about?

234
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,480
Why do you think Ma Qi did this?

235
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,279
How should I know?

236
00:12:33,559 --> 00:12:35,720
He's always been so eccentric.

237
00:12:36,159 --> 00:12:37,399
Putting yourself in his shoes again?

238
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:39,919
It shouldn't be strange, though.

239
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:43,320
However odd, there should still be some logic.

240
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:44,879
If I were Ma Qi...

241
00:12:44,879 --> 00:12:46,000
Why would I do this?

242
00:12:46,519 --> 00:12:48,480
There are a few things I just can't figure out.

243
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:50,320
What did you say just now?

244
00:12:50,679 --> 00:12:51,799
I asked if you wanted some hot water.

245
00:12:53,399 --> 00:12:54,120
No, I'm good.

246
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,159
Done thinking. Time to sleep.

247
00:12:56,399 --> 00:12:58,399
Still have to attend to Secretary-General Lin tomorrow.

248
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:01,840
We're closing the net.

249
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:07,200
Is it earlier or later than you expected?

250
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:13,879
Caught completely unprepared.

251
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:18,519
Does that mean we're off the day after tomorrow?

252
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,559
The week-long Cultural and Trade Fair

253
00:13:25,559 --> 00:13:26,919
is about to draw to a close.

254
00:13:27,639 --> 00:13:28,679
This grand event,

255
00:13:28,679 --> 00:13:32,080
themed on family ties and shared dreams,

256
00:13:32,639 --> 00:13:35,840
drew representatives from all 22 counties and cities of Taiwan, China.

257
00:13:36,159 --> 00:13:38,159
Nearly 10,000 people from all walks of life in Taiwan, China

258
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:40,440
and grassroots citizens came to Ronghai

259
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:42,879
to connect with mainland compatriots.

260
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,759
Though the days together were brief,

261
00:13:45,759 --> 00:13:48,240
they brought greater understanding across the strait,

262
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:50,080
as well as a deeper bond.

263
00:13:50,879 --> 00:13:52,600
The strait cannot sever family ties.

264
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,120
The more we interact,

265
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,919
the closer our hearts become.

266
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,360
They asked me to pass along a message.

267
00:13:58,559 --> 00:14:00,120
As soon as the Cultural and Trade Forum ends,

268
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,200
you are ordered to head back immediately.

269
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,480
And if I don't?

270
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,200
Once past the deadline,

271
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,519
if someone else comes after you,

272
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,159
they won't be as gentle as I am.

273
00:14:10,919 --> 00:14:12,320
If your cover is blown and you're arrested,

274
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:14,840
the superiors will spare no expense to save you,

275
00:14:14,919 --> 00:14:16,720
and find a way to trade for your release.

276
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,919
Tomorrow, after the event ends,

277
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,519
come by the office.

278
00:14:34,879 --> 00:14:36,240
There's a document on the desk.

279
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,519
Pick it up

280
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,159
and send it to Boss He for me.

281
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,320
Hello, viewers.

282
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,279
I'm station reporter Zhang Xiao.

283
00:14:43,279 --> 00:14:45,320
Behind me right now is

284
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:47,919
the closing ceremony of the 5th Cross-Strait Cultural and Trade Forum.

285
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,200
Today, we are deeply honored

286
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,679
to welcome noted businessman Mr. Zhang from Taiwan, China.

287
00:14:53,279 --> 00:14:54,279
Let's have a good chat later.

288
00:14:54,279 --> 00:14:55,799
Sure. Right this way, please.

289
00:14:55,799 --> 00:14:57,559
This turned out really well.

290
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:01,919
It's all thanks to District Mayor Wu's support.

291
00:15:01,919 --> 00:15:02,919
Not at all, not at all.

292
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:04,159
It's my duty. Just doing my job.

293
00:15:04,159 --> 00:15:04,879
Brother.

294
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,039
Boss.

295
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,480
Turned out great.

296
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,759
I've got a gift for you.

297
00:15:09,759 --> 00:15:10,720
Whenever it's convenient,

298
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:11,799
I'll give it to you.

299
00:15:11,799 --> 00:15:12,799
What kind of gift?

300
00:15:12,799 --> 00:15:14,120
Giving it in a place like this...

301
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,720
people might think I'm taking bribes.

302
00:15:16,879 --> 00:15:17,559
Looking so corrupt.

303
00:15:17,799 --> 00:15:18,840
How could I attract investors then?

304
00:15:19,039 --> 00:15:20,840
No one takes bribes in public anyway.

305
00:15:21,639 --> 00:15:22,759
I'm not trying to set you up.

306
00:15:23,039 --> 00:15:24,679
In the car or your office is fine.

307
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,000
Some other day.

308
00:15:27,879 --> 00:15:29,919
I'll be quite busy today.

309
00:15:29,919 --> 00:15:30,720
Make it today.

310
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,240
Where everyone will be tomorrow,

311
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,519
nobody knows.

312
00:15:33,519 --> 00:15:34,399
Don't you think?

313
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:37,919
President Pan,

314
00:15:39,399 --> 00:15:40,840
long time no see!

315
00:15:44,919 --> 00:15:45,399
Brother Xiao.

316
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,840
Looking sharp today.

317
00:15:48,639 --> 00:15:50,000
Even put on new leather shoes.

318
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,559
Are you trying to charm

319
00:15:51,759 --> 00:15:53,519
our lovely businesswomen from Taiwan, China, or what?

320
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,000
You're already Secretary-General,

321
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,200
yet you still speak so crudely.

322
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,480
After all these years,

323
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:01,039
I can't tell if you've grown dull or shrewd.

324
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:01,919
The money you're supposed to make,

325
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:02,840
you never miss a single cent.

326
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,159
But for "Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains",

327
00:16:04,159 --> 00:16:05,480
at the cross-strait exhibition,

328
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,440
you didn't charge a dime,

329
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:07,279
and even paid out of pocket.

330
00:16:07,279 --> 00:16:07,639
Why?

331
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,639
Doing charity?

332
00:16:09,039 --> 00:16:10,720
People change, you know.

333
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,759
Brother Xiao,

334
00:16:11,879 --> 00:16:13,440
don't think so badly of me.

335
00:16:14,679 --> 00:16:16,360
It's been almost 20 years since I came here.

336
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,240
In the blink of an eye,

337
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,879
I'm already nearing retirement.

338
00:16:18,879 --> 00:16:20,559
Every day, I barely know what I'm doing.

339
00:16:21,039 --> 00:16:22,440
Life is so dull.

340
00:16:22,639 --> 00:16:25,200
You have to find things to fool yourself with.

341
00:16:25,879 --> 00:16:26,840
What is there to fool yourself about?

342
00:16:27,639 --> 00:16:28,159
Let me tell you,

343
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,600
if you really can't sleep,

344
00:16:29,919 --> 00:16:31,320
just knock on my door,

345
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,120
have a drink with me,

346
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,679
and get everything off your chest.

347
00:16:33,679 --> 00:16:34,639
That'll guarantee you sleep soundly.

348
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:36,399
What about Brother Qi?

349
00:16:36,399 --> 00:16:37,399
Why didn't he come with you?

350
00:16:37,399 --> 00:16:39,080
He's been acting elusive lately.

351
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,799
I don't know where he went either.

352
00:17:05,799 --> 00:17:06,960
Ever since I was young,

353
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,559
I've had the same recurring nightmare.

354
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,160
Back when I was a kid,

355
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,759
in my hometown county,

356
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:13,519
whenever there was a major case,

357
00:17:13,519 --> 00:17:15,559
they'd hold public trials and executions.

358
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,400
On the day of the sentencing,

359
00:17:17,559 --> 00:17:19,319
the whole county would turn out in droves,

360
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,400
just like going to a fair.

361
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,720
One day, while I was still asleep,

362
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,599
my cousin and the others dragged me out,

363
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:26,200
and we ran to the execution ground.

364
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:27,920
When I got there and looked,

365
00:17:28,799 --> 00:17:30,319
a row of condemned prisoners

366
00:17:30,319 --> 00:17:31,920
were kneeling far off in the distance.

367
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,680
It was the first time I'd seen anything like it.

368
00:17:35,279 --> 00:17:37,799
Then someone felt we were too far away to see,

369
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,559
and urged us to move forward.

370
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:43,279
Step by step,

371
00:17:43,759 --> 00:17:44,839
we walked closer and closer.

372
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,480
That was when I saw a man.

373
00:17:47,799 --> 00:17:49,119
He had a placard hanging on him

374
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,279
with five words written on it:

375
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:52,880
"Kuomintang Secret Agent."

376
00:17:56,799 --> 00:17:57,839
I actually recognized him.

377
00:18:02,119 --> 00:18:03,400
He was my neighbor.

378
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:05,839
For a long time, I couldn't believe

379
00:18:06,359 --> 00:18:07,400
he was a spy.

380
00:18:08,039 --> 00:18:09,680
A man you saw every day,

381
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,799
who greeted you every day,

382
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:12,960
who was always so polite,

383
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,119
and if he saw you were in a rush,

384
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:16,000
would let you use the bathroom first.

385
00:18:16,119 --> 00:18:17,680
How could someone like that be a spy?

386
00:18:18,519 --> 00:18:20,359
When it came time for the execution,

387
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:22,000
just as the armed police officer was about to fire,

388
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,759
the gun suddenly jammed.

389
00:18:25,079 --> 00:18:26,359
He suddenly turned his head and asked,

390
00:18:26,599 --> 00:18:28,079
"Why haven't you shot yet?"

391
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:31,400
No one expected him to speak.

392
00:18:33,119 --> 00:18:34,559
Afterward, on the way out,

393
00:18:34,839 --> 00:18:36,160
everyone was saying,

394
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:37,720
"Those spies sure are something.

395
00:18:37,799 --> 00:18:39,240
They've got nerves of steel.

396
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,720
To dare to speak during an execution,

397
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,319
and even rush them to shoot!"

398
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,000
But I don't think so.

399
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,519
I think he was terrified.

400
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:51,920
Because he'd been waiting to die,

401
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,880
and the waiting broke him.

402
00:18:56,519 --> 00:18:57,400
I believe

403
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,039
that if given another chance,

404
00:18:59,519 --> 00:19:01,240
he definitely wouldn't choose to be a spy.

405
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,279
Didn't you always say

406
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:06,519
entrepreneurs are the only ones who can't turn back?

407
00:19:07,319 --> 00:19:08,319
But I don't think that's true.

408
00:19:09,319 --> 00:19:10,480
In this world,

409
00:19:11,119 --> 00:19:12,480
only spies...

410
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,400
secret agents can never turn back.

411
00:19:18,039 --> 00:19:20,039
Yet if you really think about it,

412
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,839
anyone can turn back.

413
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:30,119
Respected leaders, distinguished guests,

414
00:19:30,119 --> 00:19:32,440
and entrepreneur friends from both sides of the Strait,

415
00:19:32,559 --> 00:19:35,079
after several days of in-depth exchanges

416
00:19:35,079 --> 00:19:36,240
and earnest dialogue,

417
00:19:36,519 --> 00:19:38,240
the 5th Cultural and Trade Forum

418
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:40,599
is about to draw to a close.

419
00:19:40,839 --> 00:19:42,799
Now, please welcome

420
00:19:42,799 --> 00:19:44,720
Deputy Secretary-General of Taipei Chamber of Commerce,

421
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:47,279
Chairman of Beifeng International Trade in Services,

422
00:19:47,279 --> 00:19:48,720
Mr. Lin Kanshan,

423
00:19:56,519 --> 00:19:58,480
an outstanding representative of mainland entrepreneurs,

424
00:19:58,799 --> 00:20:00,599
President He Chunxiao,

425
00:20:02,359 --> 00:20:03,799
and our lovely students,

426
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:06,599
to recite the Tang poem together:

427
00:20:06,599 --> 00:20:07,640
"A Spring Morning."

428
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:28,200
In spring I sleep, unaware of dawn,

429
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:34,559
Everywhere birds are heard singing.

430
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:41,240
Last night came the sound of wind and rain,

431
00:20:42,039 --> 00:20:49,039
How many blossoms have fallen, I wonder?

432
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,920
All right.

433
00:22:53,319 --> 00:22:54,240
You're right.

434
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:57,359
In this world,

435
00:22:58,240 --> 00:22:59,960
only spies have no way back.

436
00:23:01,759 --> 00:23:04,160
If that person had the chance to choose again,

437
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:07,119
they definitely wouldn't choose to be an agent.

438
00:23:09,079 --> 00:23:09,880
How was that?

439
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,799
I wasn't out of tune just now, was I?

440
00:23:12,079 --> 00:23:13,240
You knew we were coming for you.

441
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,599
Why didn't you run?

442
00:23:14,799 --> 00:23:15,880
Nowhere left to run.

443
00:23:16,799 --> 00:23:18,480
I didn't expect you to be so fast.

444
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,839
And I didn't want to run anymore anyway.

445
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:25,920
What has to stay, stays.

446
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:27,720
What can't be escaped, can't be avoided.

447
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:29,720
Why bother struggling anymore?

448
00:23:31,519 --> 00:23:32,599
You're a smart man.

449
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:34,200
In business, yes.

450
00:23:34,279 --> 00:23:35,440
In getting things done, too.

451
00:23:36,799 --> 00:23:37,880
But not in how you live your life.

452
00:23:40,119 --> 00:23:41,000
It doesn't matter anymore.

453
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:43,279
Everyone...

454
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:46,519
wants to live the life they dreamed of.

455
00:23:47,079 --> 00:23:48,880
But not everyone has a choice.

456
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:50,599
Just like...

457
00:23:50,799 --> 00:23:52,279
when Wen Zongshu read our fortunes,

458
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,880
we still ended up muddling through life anyway.

459
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,559
The script of life...

460
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,240
is impossible to predict.

461
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:02,839
Do you think Wen Zongshu's reading was accurate?

462
00:24:04,599 --> 00:24:06,079
Accurate or not, it doesn't matter now.

463
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:07,599
What difference would it make even if it was?

464
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:09,119
I still ended up coming here,

465
00:24:09,599 --> 00:24:10,720
living next door to you,

466
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,079
being your neighbor.

467
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:16,480
Coming here when I was so young,

468
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:18,680
with no idea how many years I'd end up staying.

469
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,039
And now...

470
00:24:21,279 --> 00:24:22,400
I can't stay,

471
00:24:22,759 --> 00:24:23,799
and I can't go back.

472
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:25,480
That's true.

473
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:27,680
Even if you guessed right,

474
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:28,920
you'd still have to come back.

475
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:32,519
Unless you turn yourself in.

476
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:36,440
It's too late to turn myself in now.

477
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:39,440
If you want to turn back, it's never too late.

478
00:24:41,599 --> 00:24:42,920
For a nobody like me,

479
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:45,079
even if it's not too late,

480
00:24:45,759 --> 00:24:46,960
it won't change anything anyway.

481
00:24:47,720 --> 00:24:48,799
You think you didn't do anything,

482
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,400
but you actually did a lot.

483
00:24:51,519 --> 00:24:52,759
The land you requisitioned,

484
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,400
the preparations you made,

485
00:24:55,039 --> 00:24:56,200
the materials you stockpiled...

486
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:57,759
you never touched any of it.

487
00:24:58,599 --> 00:25:01,000
Plus, what you did for the Cultural and Trade Forum...

488
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:02,799
will always be remembered.

489
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:06,880
A spy must be cold-blooded and composed.

490
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:09,319
You were never cut out to be a spy.

491
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:10,400
Then what am I?

492
00:25:13,279 --> 00:25:14,359
You're my neighbor.

493
00:25:21,359 --> 00:25:22,319
I'll wait for you downstairs.

494
00:25:23,039 --> 00:25:24,279
You can ride in my car.

495
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:26,559
Don't worry, nobody knows.

496
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:29,000
You're a secretary-general, after all.

497
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,039
Let's save you some dignity.

498
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,400
Thank you all for your support.

499
00:25:59,839 --> 00:26:00,319
Thank you.

500
00:26:00,799 --> 00:26:01,440
Please keep supporting us.

501
00:26:02,079 --> 00:26:02,440
I'll take my leave now.

502
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:03,319
Thank you for your support.

503
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:41,720
Boss.

504
00:26:43,279 --> 00:26:44,079
Boss.

505
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:53,279
Your phone.

506
00:26:58,400 --> 00:26:59,680
You haven't been drinking today, right?

507
00:27:03,319 --> 00:27:05,200
Drive my car back.

508
00:27:07,839 --> 00:27:08,599
From now on,

509
00:27:09,599 --> 00:27:10,519
cut back on the drinking.

510
00:27:13,400 --> 00:27:14,559
Your license isn't expired, is it?

511
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:20,759
That's all, then.

512
00:27:22,559 --> 00:27:23,240
Boss.

513
00:27:40,519 --> 00:27:41,160
Wait a minute.

514
00:27:57,279 --> 00:27:58,960
While you're alive,

515
00:28:00,519 --> 00:28:01,640
just live your life well.

516
00:28:03,039 --> 00:28:04,240
When the day comes to die,

517
00:28:05,440 --> 00:28:06,960
then worry about what comes after.

518
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:13,640
Have the surgery.

519
00:28:15,599 --> 00:28:16,920
If something bad grew inside,

520
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:19,079
you just cut it out.

521
00:28:22,759 --> 00:28:23,960
If you really don't want to,

522
00:28:24,519 --> 00:28:26,759
just get some good food and drinks,

523
00:28:30,119 --> 00:28:31,599
and buy lots of nice clothes.

524
00:28:42,079 --> 00:28:43,519
Tell me, is this fate or what?

525
00:28:45,119 --> 00:28:46,319
The first day you met me,

526
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,680
you scammed money out of me,

527
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,240
and I've been paying for you ever since.

528
00:28:51,839 --> 00:28:53,279
Did I owe you in a past life?

529
00:28:57,599 --> 00:28:59,240
Say something. Did I?

530
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:12,519
Let's go.

531
00:30:09,200 --> 00:30:10,039
Let's go.

532
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:23,000
District Chief Wu,

533
00:31:23,799 --> 00:31:25,559
Mr. Lin's assistant brought this over,

534
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:27,480
along with a message from Mr. Lin:

535
00:31:27,920 --> 00:31:28,599
as old brothers,

536
00:31:28,759 --> 00:31:29,759
thank you for the past twenty years

537
00:31:29,759 --> 00:31:31,079
of your help and support.

538
00:31:31,279 --> 00:31:32,079
He will never forget it.

539
00:31:38,799 --> 00:31:39,720
Twenty years,

540
00:31:41,119 --> 00:31:42,599
and he's still so stingy.

541
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:46,079
To thank me,

542
00:31:47,079 --> 00:31:48,640
he just brings a few bottles of fake liquor?

543
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:51,200
Have Old Xiao arrange a meal.

544
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:52,839
I won't be joining.

545
00:31:53,599 --> 00:31:54,880
Just go and keep them company.

546
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:56,359
Director Xiao didn't come in today.

547
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:57,680
We can't reach him by phone either.

548
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,200
He didn't come?

549
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:03,359
He didn't ask me for time off.

550
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:27,640
Hello.

551
00:32:27,920 --> 00:32:30,799
The number you called is not answering.

552
00:32:31,079 --> 00:32:32,079
Please try again...

553
00:32:38,759 --> 00:32:40,680
Why haven't we left yet? What's going on?

554
00:32:40,799 --> 00:32:42,000
The engine broke down.

555
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:42,920
They're fixing it.

556
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:50,799
Skipper.

557
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:54,440
Skipper, how long until it's fixed?

558
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:57,759
What's the rush? It takes time.

559
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:59,160
Aren't you waiting for high tide anyway?

560
00:32:59,279 --> 00:33:00,759
It'll be fixed for you by 1:30, all right?

561
00:33:01,839 --> 00:33:02,960
I'm going to Xiamen.

562
00:33:03,359 --> 00:33:04,400
What... what high tide?

563
00:33:05,319 --> 00:33:06,599
I'm not going to Kinmen anymore.

564
00:33:06,920 --> 00:33:08,200
I'm not going to Taichung anymore.

565
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:24,759
Engineer Cao.

566
00:33:27,359 --> 00:33:28,920
You're Yin...

567
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:29,599
Long time no see.

568
00:33:29,599 --> 00:33:30,839
Long time no see. Long time no see.

569
00:33:31,319 --> 00:33:32,160
What are you doing?

570
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:33,400
I'm one of our own!

571
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:35,400
You're not one of our own.

572
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:39,279
No, no, no, I'm one of our own!

573
00:33:39,279 --> 00:33:40,240
I really am one of our own!

574
00:33:40,799 --> 00:33:42,039
This is a complete misunderstanding!

575
00:33:42,359 --> 00:33:43,720
I'm Master Qi's man!

576
00:33:43,839 --> 00:33:46,119
I've worked for State Security for years!

577
00:33:46,119 --> 00:33:46,920
Who is Master Qi?

578
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:47,799
Ma Qi!

579
00:33:47,799 --> 00:33:50,160
Ma Qi hasn't been with State Security for a long time.

580
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:52,519
Drive.

581
00:33:55,759 --> 00:33:56,839
Comrades,

582
00:33:56,839 --> 00:33:59,240
I have good news to announce.

583
00:33:59,240 --> 00:33:59,880
Recently,

584
00:34:00,319 --> 00:34:02,880
at the Xichang Satellite Launch Center,

585
00:34:03,240 --> 00:34:05,839
using a Long March 3B carrier rocket,

586
00:34:06,039 --> 00:34:09,519
our country successfully launched

587
00:34:09,519 --> 00:34:10,719
the Chang'e 3 lunar probe into space.

588
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:13,519
The Chang'e 3 probe has successfully

589
00:34:13,519 --> 00:34:15,880
achieved our first soft landing on the Moon

590
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:18,000
and lunar surface rover exploration,

591
00:34:18,239 --> 00:34:21,039
opening, one might say,

592
00:34:21,239 --> 00:34:23,960
a brand-new chapter for our lunar exploration program.

593
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:36,360
Let's talk in the office.

594
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:37,119
In the office.

595
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:41,800
Take it easy.

596
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:42,760
Easy, take it easy.

597
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:43,239
Behave yourself.

598
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,280
Comrade, comrade, take it easy.

599
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:44,800
Easy now.

600
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:04,519
What are you doing?!

601
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:06,760
I didn't do anything! Why are you arresting me?

602
00:35:06,920 --> 00:35:07,559
Freeze! Don't move!

603
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:08,679
Don't move!

604
00:35:09,239 --> 00:35:10,239
What are you grabbing me for?!

605
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:11,519
What do you think you're doing?!

606
00:35:11,519 --> 00:35:12,559
Don't move! Stay still!

607
00:35:24,119 --> 00:35:24,760
Take him away.

608
00:35:27,159 --> 00:35:27,800
Don't move.

609
00:35:28,039 --> 00:35:28,679
Ma Qi!

610
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:30,639
Ma Qi!

611
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:19,400
Thanks.

612
00:36:24,719 --> 00:36:25,960
What kind of person do you think

613
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:28,519
Lin Kanshan really was?

614
00:36:32,159 --> 00:36:33,599
You must think

615
00:36:33,599 --> 00:36:34,719
he was a bad man,

616
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,239
someone who deserved to die.

617
00:36:39,079 --> 00:36:40,960
In truth, he didn't want it to end like this either.

618
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:45,000
He had no choice.

619
00:36:47,480 --> 00:36:48,639
There was nothing he could do.

620
00:36:57,480 --> 00:36:59,679
If you're cold, let's head back.

621
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:18,920
From the day I first met Lin Kanshan,

622
00:37:20,039 --> 00:37:21,719
everything he's ever done

623
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:23,639
is in this notebook.

624
00:37:36,079 --> 00:37:37,559
Let's go. Let's head back.

625
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,199
Stay a little longer.

626
00:37:42,039 --> 00:37:42,880
Stay with me a bit longer.

627
00:37:43,679 --> 00:37:44,480
Just for a moment.

628
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:52,119
Ma Qi.

629
00:38:53,679 --> 00:38:55,960
Have you figured out what he's thinking?

630
00:39:00,679 --> 00:39:01,840
Let me tell you a story.

631
00:39:02,599 --> 00:39:03,480
Hear me out.

632
00:39:05,719 --> 00:39:06,360
We have infiltrated them,

633
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:07,280
and they have infiltrated us.

634
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:08,239
In this cross-strait chess match,

635
00:39:08,239 --> 00:39:10,199
a single move often takes over a decade.

636
00:39:10,199 --> 00:39:11,559
If Lin Kanshan could be planted here,

637
00:39:12,079 --> 00:39:13,039
then why couldn't

638
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:14,880
one of ours cross over?

639
00:39:15,199 --> 00:39:16,599
It takes ten years to blossom,

640
00:39:16,599 --> 00:39:17,880
and ten years to bear fruit.

641
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:19,400
After Li Fengge was compromised,

642
00:39:19,400 --> 00:39:21,159
the MIB wanted to find a replacement.

643
00:39:21,159 --> 00:39:23,119
Who could be more suitable than Ma Qi?

644
00:39:23,119 --> 00:39:24,280
He's a rebel to the bone,

645
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:26,199
with countless reprimands on his record.

646
00:39:26,199 --> 00:39:27,079
Full of grievances,

647
00:39:27,079 --> 00:39:28,000
breaking all the rules.

648
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:29,119
He always wanted to be the spear,

649
00:39:29,199 --> 00:39:30,679
yet he was forced to act as the shield.

650
00:39:30,679 --> 00:39:31,960
Among all the impenetrable eggs in the bureau,

651
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:34,599
his shell alone was full of cracks.

652
00:39:34,599 --> 00:39:35,559
If I were Zhu Yingjia,

653
00:39:35,559 --> 00:39:37,079
I would've targeted him too.

654
00:39:37,079 --> 00:39:38,119
So, planning ahead,

655
00:39:38,119 --> 00:39:40,159
the seduction began back in the nineties.

656
00:39:40,159 --> 00:39:41,880
On the mainland, in Hong Kong, China,

657
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:44,159
Yang Shiwen was the most dedicated broker.

658
00:39:44,360 --> 00:39:45,960
You think Ma Qi did it intentionally?

659
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:48,400
Including leaving marks on the doorframe next door.

660
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:49,519
Why did he help Lin Kanshan?

661
00:39:49,519 --> 00:39:50,519
To present a pledge of loyalty.

662
00:39:50,519 --> 00:39:52,199
Why make errors? Why resign?

663
00:39:52,199 --> 00:39:54,480
To find the right opening to switch sides.

664
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:55,800
Why did he become an intelligence broker?

665
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:57,679
Only then could he step outside.

666
00:39:57,840 --> 00:39:59,880
Only then could he tap cross-strait intel flows.

667
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:01,519
Why did he play hard to get with Taipei?

668
00:40:01,519 --> 00:40:03,280
Because he was driving a hard bargain.

669
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:04,960
Why did he get mixed up with Wen Zongshu?

670
00:40:04,960 --> 00:40:06,639
To learn every detail about him.

671
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:08,760
He needed to open a new channel

672
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:10,079
to funnel operational funds for the MIB.

673
00:40:10,079 --> 00:40:11,400
That was how he built trust.

674
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:12,840
Why did he approach Cao Liaoping?

675
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:14,400
Because Old Jia, for all these years,

676
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:15,960
had been leaking intelligence to the outside.

677
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:17,039
He needed a specialist

678
00:40:17,039 --> 00:40:18,440
to alter the parameters for him.

679
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:19,960
Why didn't they arrest Old Jia?

680
00:40:20,199 --> 00:40:21,679
They only blocked Wen Zongshu's intelligence

681
00:40:21,679 --> 00:40:22,639
and spared the man.

682
00:40:22,639 --> 00:40:24,920
To cure Taiwan, China of a malignant disease.

683
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,559
They had to feed them medicine and food.

684
00:40:26,559 --> 00:40:27,239
Why did Old Wei

685
00:40:27,239 --> 00:40:28,800
insist on keeping this man in his grip?

686
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:29,840
Because he couldn't hand him to the Second Division.

687
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:31,760
He had to run him through Ma Qi's channel.

688
00:40:31,920 --> 00:40:33,079
Why approach Jin Chizhong

689
00:40:33,280 --> 00:40:34,119
and Lu Zhifei?

690
00:40:34,239 --> 00:40:35,440
To process intelligence,

691
00:40:35,639 --> 00:40:36,440
maintain communications,

692
00:40:36,679 --> 00:40:37,880
and control the pace.

693
00:40:38,039 --> 00:40:39,519
Even without approaching the two of them,

694
00:40:39,519 --> 00:40:40,960
they would've slipped up sooner or later.

695
00:40:41,079 --> 00:40:42,360
A man like Ma Qi,

696
00:40:42,920 --> 00:40:44,880
with brains, experience, and resources—

697
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:45,840
if he truly wanted to flee,

698
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:47,400
whether overseas or to Taiwan, China,

699
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:48,760
Qiao Liang or Zhu Yingjia

700
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:50,199
would have arranged the most flawless

701
00:40:50,199 --> 00:40:51,320
escape route and extraction plan.

702
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:53,480
It'd be far more discreet and seamless than this.

703
00:40:53,480 --> 00:40:54,800
So why did he surrender without resistance?

704
00:40:56,039 --> 00:40:57,480
When he walked into the interrogation room,

705
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:58,639
it was like returning home.

706
00:40:59,039 --> 00:41:01,599
He was even more relaxed than outside.

707
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:02,679
Because he knows

708
00:41:02,679 --> 00:41:04,400
these handcuffs are his insurance policy.

709
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:05,000
Only this way

710
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:06,559
will Taipei trust him even more.

711
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:09,719
The detention center is a stepping stone. Climb it,

712
00:41:09,880 --> 00:41:11,559
and he can reach the MIB's top brass.

713
00:41:11,559 --> 00:41:12,960
Why didn't Old Wei say anything?

714
00:41:12,960 --> 00:41:14,159
Because of confidentiality.

715
00:41:14,559 --> 00:41:15,880
Not a single word could be spoken.

716
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:17,559
But the provincial department must know.

717
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:19,679
Director Wu must know as well.

718
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:20,599
After he retired,

719
00:41:20,599 --> 00:41:21,639
Old Wei certainly knew too.

720
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:23,199
And now, you know as well.

721
00:41:30,480 --> 00:41:31,400
What are you doing?

722
00:41:33,480 --> 00:41:34,960
Today is such a special day.

723
00:41:35,880 --> 00:41:37,000
Shouldn't we celebrate?

724
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:42,320
We're out of liquor.

725
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:44,360
I'll go buy some for you.

726
00:42:00,239 --> 00:42:01,360
We've been working a lot of overtime lately,

727
00:42:01,719 --> 00:42:03,000
so the cafeteria closes late, too.

728
00:42:04,599 --> 00:42:06,760
That's how I got you a bowl of handmade noodles.

729
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:09,639
Unlike when we interrogated Cao Leping,

730
00:42:09,639 --> 00:42:11,039
when we had to settle for instant noodles.

731
00:42:11,760 --> 00:42:13,159
One bite and I knew it was Lao Gu's cooking.

732
00:42:13,159 --> 00:42:14,159
Still as salty as ever.

733
00:42:15,119 --> 00:42:15,679
Is that enough?

734
00:42:16,159 --> 00:42:17,440
Want me to get you another bowl?

735
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:19,840
No more. It's too salty.

736
00:42:20,800 --> 00:42:21,320
Got any liquor?

737
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:22,880
Sorghum liquor would be best.

738
00:42:23,320 --> 00:42:24,079
If that's not possible,

739
00:42:24,599 --> 00:42:25,559
rice wine will do.

740
00:42:26,519 --> 00:42:27,360
To wet my throat,

741
00:42:27,360 --> 00:42:28,280
then we can keep talking.

742
00:42:32,159 --> 00:42:33,920
Don't tell me you don't even have the authority for that.

743
00:42:35,719 --> 00:42:37,000
Why don't you go ask for approval?

744
00:42:37,239 --> 00:42:38,559
Why the hell should I?

745
00:42:40,559 --> 00:42:41,079
That's enough.

746
00:42:42,119 --> 00:42:42,639
Go on.

747
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:45,760
You want to play games?

748
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:47,280
I'll play with you.

749
00:42:58,079 --> 00:42:59,920
Clearly, this wasn't planned in advance.

750
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:01,880
Get him out of the way.

751
00:43:01,880 --> 00:43:03,039
What do you want to say to me?

752
00:43:08,159 --> 00:43:09,239
I'm Wang Kai,

753
00:43:09,239 --> 00:43:10,960
inviting you to watch the TV series

754
00:43:10,960 --> 00:43:11,880
*Confrontation.*

755
00:43:12,039 --> 00:43:14,199
You went to great lengths to guide me on this path,

756
00:43:14,199 --> 00:43:15,519
only to defect halfway through.

757
00:43:15,840 --> 00:43:17,719
You were the mentor I respected most,

758
00:43:17,920 --> 00:43:19,840
yet you became the enemy I must investigate.

759
00:43:20,320 --> 00:43:21,199
In recent years,

760
00:43:21,199 --> 00:43:22,599
the MIB has kept ordering me

761
00:43:22,599 --> 00:43:24,719
to acquire land near the dual-use airport.

762
00:43:24,719 --> 00:43:27,599
In fact, they're building an underground tunnel.

763
00:43:27,599 --> 00:43:28,719
If war ever breaks out,

764
00:43:28,719 --> 00:43:30,400
they can blow up the airport runway.

765
00:43:30,920 --> 00:43:33,800
After all that effort, both on and behind the scenes,

766
00:43:33,800 --> 00:43:35,159
have you ever considered

767
00:43:35,159 --> 00:43:36,239
that all these years in prison

768
00:43:36,559 --> 00:43:37,480
might be for nothing?
